tlaps-bench — third-party attributions
======================================

tlaps-bench itself is released under the MIT License (see LICENSE). The
benchmark is built from TLA+ specifications written by third parties; this file
records their provenance and the original copyright/license notices. Some
generated benchmark tasks remove source comments and therefore may not carry the
upstream in-file license headers. Third-party material remains under its
applicable upstream license; the protocols and proof obligations are unchanged.

Benchmark groups live under benchmark/proof-completion/ (proof completion) and
benchmark/proof-from-scratch/ (proof from scratch).
Full license texts for Apache-2.0 and BSD-2-Clause material are provided in
LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt and LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause.txt, respectively.


== Benchmark specifications ==

MongoDB distributed transactions — benchmark group MongoDB
    MultiShardTxn.tla, Storage.tla, ClientCentric.tla, and Util.tla are copied
    unchanged from mongodb-labs/vldb25-dist-txns at commit
    7e299d4bc94ef9cdd24e91985944bb1e46623601:
    https://github.com/mongodb-labs/vldb25-dist-txns/tree/7e299d4bc94ef9cdd24e91985944bb1e46623601
    Artifact for William Schultz and Murat Demirbas, "Design and Modular
    Verification of Distributed Transactions in MongoDB" (PVLDB 2025).
    No repository-wide license file is present at this revision; these
    materials are not relicensed under this repository's MIT license.
    ClientCentric.tla credits Tim Soethout and identifies its BSD-2-Clause
    source as https://github.com/cwi-swat/tla-ci. Its license is preserved in
    LICENSES/tla-ci-BSD-2-Clause.txt (Copyright 2020, ING Bank / CWI), copied
    from tla-ci at da10d932270879f5e9d21eb3ed192b2d57d99109.
    Util.tla credits Stephan Merz for PermSeqs, from "TLA+ Case Study:
    A Resource Allocator" (2004).
    MultiShardTxnSnapshot.tla is a local theorem wrapper that selects the
    upstream snapshot settings. No reference proof is supplied.

